#: ../../source/templates_ollama.md:16
msgid "1. Visual Theme & Atmosphere"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_ollama.md:18
msgid ""
"Ollama's interface is radical minimalism taken to its logical conclusion "
"— a pure-white void where content floats without decoration, shadow, or "
"color. The design philosophy mirrors the product itself: strip away "
"everything unnecessary until only the essential tool remains. This is the"
" digital equivalent of a Dieter Rams object — every pixel earns its "
"place, and the absence of design IS the design."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_ollama.md:20
msgid ""
"The entire page exists in pure grayscale. There is zero chromatic color "
"in the interface — no brand blue, no accent green, no semantic red. The "
"only colors that exist are shades between pure black (`#000000`) and pure"
" white (`#ffffff`), creating a monochrome environment that lets the "
"user's mental model of \"open models\" remain uncolored by brand opinion."
" The Ollama llama mascot, rendered in simple black line art, is the only "
"illustration — and even it's monochrome."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_ollama.md:22
msgid ""
"What makes Ollama distinctive is the combination of SF Pro Rounded "
"(Apple's rounded system font) with an exclusively pill-shaped geometry "
"(9999px radius on everything interactive). The rounded letterforms + "
"rounded buttons + rounded containers create a cohesive \"softness "
"language\" that makes a developer CLI tool feel approachable and friendly"
" rather than intimidating. This is minimalism with warmth — not cold "
"Swiss-style grid minimalism, but the kind where the edges are literally "
"softened."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_ollama.md:24
msgid "**Key Characteristics:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_ollama.md:25
msgid "Pure white canvas with zero chromatic color — completely grayscale"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_ollama.md:26
msgid "SF Pro Rounded headlines creating a distinctively Apple-like softness"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_ollama.md:27
msgid ""
"Binary border-radius system: 12px (containers) or 9999px (everything "
"interactive)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_ollama.md:28
msgid ""
"Zero shadows — depth comes exclusively from background color shifts and "
"borders"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_ollama.md:29
msgid ""
"Pill-shaped geometry on all interactive elements (buttons, tabs, inputs, "
"tags)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_ollama.md:30
msgid "The Ollama llama as the sole illustration — black line art, no color"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_ollama.md:31
msgid ""
"Extreme content restraint — the homepage is short, focused, and "
"uncluttered"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_ollama.md:33
msgid "2. Color Palette & Roles"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_ollama.md:35
msgid "Primary"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_ollama.md:36
msgid ""
"**Pure Black** (`#000000`): Primary headlines, primary links, and the "
"darkest text. The only \"color\" that demands attention."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_ollama.md:37
msgid ""
"**Near Black** (`#262626`): Button text on light surfaces, secondary "
"headline weight."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_ollama.md:38
msgid ""
"**Darkest Surface** (`#090909`): The darkest possible surface — barely "
"distinguishable from pure black, used for footer or dark containers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_ollama.md:40
msgid "Surface & Background"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_ollama.md:41
msgid ""
"**Pure White** (`#ffffff`): The primary page background — not off-white, "
"not cream, pure white. Button surfaces for secondary actions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_ollama.md:42
msgid ""
"**Snow** (`#fafafa`): The subtlest possible surface distinction from "
"white — used for section backgrounds and barely-elevated containers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_ollama.md:43
msgid ""
"**Light Gray** (`#e5e5e5`): Button backgrounds, borders, and the primary "
"containment color. The workhorse neutral."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_ollama.md:45
msgid "Neutrals & Text"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_ollama.md:46
msgid ""
"**Stone** (`#737373`): Secondary body text, footer links, and de-"
"emphasized content. The primary \"muted\" tone."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_ollama.md:47
msgid ""
"**Mid Gray** (`#525252`): Emphasized secondary text, slightly darker than"
" Stone."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_ollama.md:48
msgid ""
"**Silver** (`#a3a3a3`): Tertiary text, placeholders, and deeply de-"
"emphasized metadata."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_ollama.md:49
msgid "**Button Text Dark** (`#404040`): Specific to white-surface button text."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_ollama.md:51
msgid "Semantic & Accent"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_ollama.md:52
msgid ""
"**Ring Blue** (`#3b82f6` at 50%): The ONLY non-gray color in the entire "
"system — Tailwind's default focus ring, used exclusively for keyboard "
"accessibility. Never visible in normal interaction flow."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_ollama.md:53
msgid ""
"**Border Light** (`#d4d4d4`): A slightly darker gray for white-surface "
"button borders."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_ollama.md:55
msgid "Gradient System"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_ollama.md:56
msgid ""
"**None.** Ollama uses absolutely no gradients. Visual separation comes "
"from flat color blocks and single-pixel borders. This is a deliberate, "
"almost philosophical design choice."
msgstr ""

