#: ../../source/templates_ollama.md:200
msgid ""
"**Shadow Philosophy**: Ollama uses **zero shadows**. This is not an "
"oversight — it's a deliberate design decision. Every other major AI "
"product site uses at least subtle shadows. Ollama's flat, shadowless "
"approach creates a paper-like experience where elements are distinguished"
" purely by background color and single-pixel borders. Depth is "
"communicated through **content hierarchy and typography weight**, not "
"visual layering."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_ollama.md:202
msgid "7. Do's and Don'ts"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_ollama.md:204
msgid "Do"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_ollama.md:205
msgid ""
"Use pure white (`#ffffff`) as the page background — never off-white or "
"cream"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_ollama.md:206
msgid ""
"Use pill-shaped (9999px) radius on all interactive elements — buttons, "
"tabs, inputs, tags"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_ollama.md:207
msgid ""
"Use 12px radius on all non-interactive containers — code blocks, cards, "
"panels"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_ollama.md:208
msgid ""
"Keep the palette strictly grayscale — no chromatic colors except the blue"
" focus ring"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_ollama.md:209
msgid ""
"Use SF Pro Rounded at weight 500 for display headings — the rounded "
"terminals are the brand expression"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_ollama.md:210
msgid ""
"Maintain zero shadows — depth comes from borders and background shifts "
"only"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_ollama.md:211
msgid "Keep content density low — each section should present one clear idea"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_ollama.md:212
msgid ""
"Use monospace for terminal commands and code — it's primary content, not "
"decoration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_ollama.md:213
msgid ""
"Keep all buttons at 10px 24px padding with pill shape — consistency is "
"absolute"
